1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,377
Hey.
Hi.

2
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:03,879
Who wants French toast?

3
00:00:03,921 --> 00:00:05,756
Oh, I'll have some.
Me, too.

4
00:00:05,798 --> 00:00:08,550
Eggs and milk
in the fridge. Thanks.

5
00:00:08,592 --> 00:00:09,969
Ow!

6
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,428
What's the matter, honey?

7
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:12,680
My hand feels weird.

8
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,765
I guess it's because
I'm engaged!

9
00:00:14,807 --> 00:00:16,433
How long before

10
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:18,059
that starts getting annoying?

11
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:19,227
Starts?

12
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:22,815
So, let's actually get started
on the wedding plans.

13
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:23,858
Okay.

14
00:00:23,899 --> 00:00:24,900
Already?

15
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:26,527
Yeah, we got a lot to do.

16
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,612
We got to think about flowers,
the caterers, the music.

17
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:29,655
I have thoughts on that.

18
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:31,657
Oh, Chandler, too many cooks.

19
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,994
Take it from me. As the groom

20
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,621
all you have to do is show up
and try to say the right name.

21
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,375
Okay.

22
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:43,335
What in God's name is that?

23
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:45,420
Oh, my God.
The wedding book?

24
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:48,007
I haven't seen that
since the fourth grade.

25
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:50,592
Monica:
This baby has
got everything.

26
00:00:50,634 --> 00:00:53,178
Take, you know,
locations, for instance:

27
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:56,765
first organized alphabetically,
then geographically

28
00:00:56,807 --> 00:00:59,852
then by square footage.

29
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:02,563
That is so smart.

30
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,523
( softly ):
Break it off.

31
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:06,567
( coughs ):
Break it off now.

32
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:17,619
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

33
00:01:17,661 --> 00:01:19,663
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

34
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:22,791
♪ Your love life's DOA ♪

35
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:27,504
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

36
00:01:27,546 --> 00:01:29,673
♪ When it hasn't been your day ♪

37
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:33,134
♪ Your week, your month,
or even your year ♪

38
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:36,471
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

39
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:42,728
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

40
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:49,234
And that should
conclusively prove

41
00:01:49,276 --> 00:01:53,154
that I had the idea
for Jurassic Park first.

42
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,698
Now, let's...
Hey, Ross.

43
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,950
Phoebe, oh, my God.

44
00:01:55,991 --> 00:01:58,077
What are you doing here?

45
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,954
I need to talk to you.
It's pretty urgent.

46
00:01:59,995 --> 00:02:01,288
It's about Monica
and Chandler.

47
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:02,623
Oh, my God.

48
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,165
Of course.

49
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:06,961
Would you please
excuse me for a moment?

50
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:09,379
Do you know
each other's hometowns?

51
00:02:09,421 --> 00:02:10,798
Why don't you...?

52
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:13,801
What's going on?

53
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,803
Well, not much, but
I was just thinking

54
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:18,221
that since those guys
just got engaged

55
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:20,808
that maybe it'd
be nice if they had
some privacy, you know?

56
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:23,184
So, could I just
move in with you

57
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:24,311
for a couple days?

58
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:28,440
Um, okay. Yeah, sure

59
00:02:28,482 --> 00:02:30,943
but what's wrong
with Monica and Chandler?

60
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:34,321
Nothing. Why?

61
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:37,116
Phoebe, you said it was urgent.

62
00:02:37,156 --> 00:02:38,826
Oh, yeah, it is. I'm
going to the movies

63
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,494
and it starts in,
like, five minutes.

64
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:44,999
Do you realize

65
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,835
I have a classroom
full of students?

66
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:51,463
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm so rude.

67
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:54,173
Does anyone want to come
to the movies?

68
00:02:58,053 --> 00:03:00,597
All right, I haven't cleared
the budget with my parents yet

69
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:02,099
but tell me how
this is for music.

70
00:03:02,141 --> 00:03:03,266
Okay.

71
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:04,893
A string quartet
for the processional

72
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:06,687
a jazz trio
for cocktails

73
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:09,690
the Bay City Rollers
for dancing... wait.

74
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:12,275
That was for my
sixth-grade wedding.

75
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:13,986
Well, you couldn't
get them, anyway.

76
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:16,697
I mean, Ian doesn't even
play anymore and Derek...

77
00:03:18,532 --> 00:03:21,200
Well, Derek is a name
I shouldn't know.

78
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:23,704
Hey, Mon, do you have
another pillow?

79
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:26,040
You know,
something a little snugglier?

80
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:29,376
Why are you napping over here
instead of over at your place?

81
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:30,544
The duck.

82
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:31,962
What? The duck?

83
00:03:32,004 --> 00:03:34,339
What the hell did
the damn duck do now?

84
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:39,761
Uh, well, he did not
get sick somewhere in there

85
00:03:39,803 --> 00:03:43,140
and it was immediately found
and properly cleaned up.

86
00:03:44,432 --> 00:03:46,018
Now do I get
to look at this book

87
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:47,394
or is it just for people

88
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,521
who are actually involved
in the wedding?

89
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:51,606
Of course
you can look at it.

90
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:53,025
Yeah, I want
your opinion, too.

91
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:54,026
Okay.

92
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:55,234
Here you go.

93
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:56,570
What do you think
about centerpieces?

94
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,696
Centerpieces.
Yeah.

95
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,489
Roses... or lilies?

96
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:00,866
Definitely roses.

97
00:04:04,745 --> 00:04:07,206
Well, I just think they're
a little bit more weddingy.

98
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,877
But lilies are the clear choice.

99
00:04:11,919 --> 00:04:14,129
Oh, my God.
It's like one mind.

100
00:04:14,171 --> 00:04:16,090
Uh-huh.

101
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:17,883
Guys, guys...

102
00:04:17,925 --> 00:04:20,385
you got to let me nap.

103
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:23,055
I'm going to get cranky.

104
00:04:23,097 --> 00:04:27,226
Joey, there is a perfectly
good couch across the hall.

105
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:30,062
Yes, it is perfectly good...

106
00:04:30,104 --> 00:04:33,440
and it is not one of the places
the duck got sick.

107
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,650
What?

108
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:37,318
All right, I'm going to go.

109
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,737
Joey

110
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:40,239
what did the duck do?

111
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:43,117
I don't know, but
he did not eat
your face cream.

112
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,755
Hey, little buddy.

113
00:04:56,797 --> 00:04:58,298
How you feeling? Ah!

114
00:05:01,468 --> 00:05:03,845
What the hell
is in that face cream?

115
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:19,820
That's so soft.

116
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:24,658
Pillowcases.

117
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:26,285
Oh, yeah...

118
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:31,165
Oh, oh... oh...

119
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:36,544
What the...?

120
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:42,009
"Zelda looked at
the chimney sweep.

121
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,511
Her father, the vicar..."

122
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:47,472
Vicar? Hmm.

123
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:49,683
"...wouldn't be home for hours.

124
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,893
"Her loins were burning.

125
00:05:51,935 --> 00:05:53,937
"She threw caution to the wind

126
00:05:53,979 --> 00:05:56,397
and reached out
and grabbed his..."

127
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:59,484
Whoa!

128
00:05:59,526 --> 00:06:01,736
Whoa.

129
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,571
This is a dirty book.

130
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:19,587
Uh, Phoebe?

131
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:21,422
( deep, sultry voice ):
Oh, Ross, hi.

132
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:25,510
Phoebe, what
are you doing?

133
00:06:25,552 --> 00:06:26,511
I'm sorry.

134
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,846
I'm with a client right now.

135
00:06:27,888 --> 00:06:29,681
Phoebe!

136
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:31,683
Okay, let's talk outside.

137
00:06:33,352 --> 00:06:35,520
Phoebe, you can't
massage people

138
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:36,730
in my apartment.

139
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,023
What's the big deal?

140
00:06:38,065 --> 00:06:39,398
I did it
at Monica and Chandler's.

141
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,650
And they knew about it?

142
00:06:44,363 --> 00:06:47,657
Okay, look, Ross,
what is this really about?

143
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:49,284
Look, this is my home

144
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:52,079
and I want to be able
to come and go whenever I want.

145
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,872
Okay, I will find
someplace else

146
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,707
to do the rest
of my appointments.

147
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:57,625
I just don't know
what the big deal is.

148
00:06:57,667 --> 00:07:00,545
The big deal is, I don't want
naked, greasy strangers

149
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:03,673
in my apartment when I want
to kick back with a puzzle...

150
00:07:03,715 --> 00:07:05,717
beer-- cold beer.

151
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:08,678
Hey.

152
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,222
Hey, Joey. What
are you doing?

153
00:07:10,264 --> 00:07:11,390
Sweeping.

154
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:14,433
Why? Does it turn you on?

155
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:17,604
No.

156
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:19,606
Hmm...

157
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:23,944
What if I was, uh,
sweeping a chimney?

158
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,447
Joey, did you eat my face cream?

159
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,326
Where you going?

160
00:07:31,368 --> 00:07:33,620
The vicar won't be home
for hours.

161
00:07:39,126 --> 00:07:43,546
Joey... where did you
learn that word?

162
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:48,260
Where do you think...

163
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:49,594
Zelda?

164
00:07:49,636 --> 00:07:51,972
( gasps )

165
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:54,141
You found my book?

166
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,310
Yeah, I did!

167
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:58,270
Joey, what-what
are you doing

168
00:07:58,312 --> 00:07:59,813
going into my bedroom?

169
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:00,855
Okay, I'm sorry.

170
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:02,399
I went in there to take a nap

171
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:04,609
and I know I shouldn't have,
but you got porn.

172
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:06,153
Oh!
You... hey, you know what?

173
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,321
I don't care.

174
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:09,030
I'm not ashamed of my book.

175
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:12,075
There's nothing wrong with
a woman enjoying a little...

176
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,743
erotica.

177
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:17,747
It's just a healthy expression
of female sexuality

178
00:08:17,789 --> 00:08:22,919
which, by the way, is something
that you will never understand.

179
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:26,714
You got porn.

180
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:28,591
( laughing )

181
00:08:36,975 --> 00:08:39,102
( yells )

182
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:41,980
( knocking at door )

183
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:49,737
Hello.

184
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:50,905
Hi.

185
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,324
Is, uh, Phoebe here?

186
00:08:52,366 --> 00:08:54,909
Uh, no, no.
Sh-she's out for the night.

187
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,536
Oh, great.

188
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:59,706
Can I... can I help you
with something?

189
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:00,707
Oh, I don't know.

190
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:01,875
Are you a masseur?

191
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:04,669
Yes, I am.

192
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:07,005
Great.

193
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:08,465
Dad?

194
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:15,055
Thank you so much.

195
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:16,931
I'll be back to
pick him up
in an hour.

196
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:26,274
So, Chandler, your parents
must have been thrilled

197
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:27,942
when you told them
you were engaged.

198
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:30,820
Oh, yeah, I should
probably call them.

199
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,572
I remember when we
first got engaged.

200
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:33,740
Oh, I don't think

201
00:09:33,781 --> 00:09:34,866
I've ever heard
that story.

202
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:36,117
Dad, really,
you don't need...

203
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:38,537
Well, I had gotten Judy
pregnant.

204
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:40,663
I still
don't know

205
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:41,873
how that happened.

206
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:43,917
You don't know
how that happened?

207
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:46,878
Your dog thought my diaphragm
was a chew toy.

208
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:50,298
What a sweet story.

209
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:52,342
Well, at least
you're not
hearing it

210
00:09:52,384 --> 00:09:55,429
for the first time at your
fifth-grade Halloween party.

211
00:09:55,470 --> 00:09:57,389
What? They wanted a scary story.

212
00:09:57,431 --> 00:09:59,516
( chuckling )

213
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:01,851
Anyway, we're really excited
about our wedding plans

214
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:04,396
and I guess pretty soon
we'll be making a big withdrawal

215
00:10:04,438 --> 00:10:05,813
from the Monica wedding fund.

216
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,482
( Monica and Chandler chuckle)

217
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:10,360
Uh-oh.

218
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:11,570
What?

219
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:13,196
You tell her, Jack,
I can't do it.

220
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:15,949
You still have the Monica
wedding fund, don't you?

221
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,325
We have it.

222
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:19,453
Only now we call it
"the beach house."

223
00:10:23,290 --> 00:10:25,333
I can't believe you spent
my wedding fund

224
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:26,334
on the beach house!

225
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:27,710
We're sorry, honey

226
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,254
but we just assumed
if you got married

227
00:10:29,296 --> 00:10:31,131
after you turned 30,
you'd pay for it yourself.

228
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,925
You bought the beach house
when I was 23.

229
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:36,303
Which means you had
seven years of beach fun

230
00:10:36,344 --> 00:10:38,763
and you can't put
a price on that, sweetie.

231
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,268
We really do feel bad
about this, though.

232
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:45,645
We started saving again
when you were dating Richard

233
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:48,189
but then that went to hell,
so we re-did the kitchen.

234
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:52,527
What about when
I started dating Chandler?

235
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:53,903
Well, it was Chandler.

236
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:55,238
We didn't think
he'd ever propose.

237
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,782
Clearly, I did not start
drinking enough

238
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,493
at the start of the meal.

239
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:00,827
( chuckling )

240
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:02,036
I can't believe it.

241
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:03,163
There is no money
for my wedding?

242
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,581
We might still have
some money

243
00:11:04,623 --> 00:11:06,541
if your father hadn't thought
it was a good idea

244
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:07,834
to sell ice
over the Internet.

245
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:09,336
It seemed like such
a simple idea.

246
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:10,504
"Stupid," Jack.

247
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:11,670
The word is "stupid."

248
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:13,047
All right, enough.

249
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:15,175
I don't want to hear
about it anymore.

250
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:17,385
Good luck, Chandler.

251
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:42,536
Okay.

252
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:45,872
Now, I'm going to...

253
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:49,042
touch you.

254
00:11:58,218 --> 00:12:00,512
Oh, that's soft.

255
00:12:25,537 --> 00:12:26,580
I can't believe this.

256
00:12:26,621 --> 00:12:27,788
Do you think

257
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,374
that your parents
can help pay for it?

258
00:12:29,416 --> 00:12:30,500
I don't know.

259
00:12:30,542 --> 00:12:32,751
My mother spent
most of her money

260
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,337
on her fourth wedding

261
00:12:34,379 --> 00:12:37,382
and she's saving the rest
for her divorce.

262
00:12:37,424 --> 00:12:39,758
And any extra cash my father has

263
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:45,223
he saves for his yearly trips
to... Dollywood.

264
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:48,226
Well, what happened at dinner?

265
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:50,562
My parents spent the money
for our wedding.

266
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:51,563
( gasps )

267
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:52,606
My God!

268
00:12:52,647 --> 00:12:53,981
What did you order?

269
00:12:56,234 --> 00:12:57,818
Wait, but... there's no money?

270
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:59,362
Well, this is terrible!

271
00:12:59,404 --> 00:13:01,780
You guys are going to have
to get married in, like

272
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:03,908
a rec center.

273
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,243
Honey, it's
going to be okay.

274
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:07,287
No, no, it's not.
It's not going to be okay.

275
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,913
It sucks!

276
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,999
No swing band, no lilies...

277
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,167
No, you know what?

278
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:14,377
It's going to be okay.

279
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:15,962
I mean, you don't need
to have this...

280
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:19,048
rustic Italian feast, you know?

281
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:23,637
And-and you don't need
this custom-made, empire-waisted

282
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:25,472
duchess satin gown.

283
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,724
You can wear off-the-rack.

284
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,647
Look, it really is

285
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:35,189
going to be okay.

286
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:37,317
The important thing
is that we love each other

287
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:39,152
and that we're going
to get married.

288
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:43,030
Do you even understand
what "off-the-rack" means?

289
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:45,366
Look, why
don't you

290
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:47,034
just pay for it yourself?

291
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,662
How? I don't have
any money.

292
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:49,996
Well, I have some.

293
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:50,829
How much?

294
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:52,165
Well, close to...

295
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,261
Wow! Are you
kidding me?

296
00:14:05,303 --> 00:14:07,013
Well, what?
How-how much is it?

297
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:08,847
It's enough
for wedding scenario "A."

298
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:10,057
( gasping ):
Really?

299
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:12,185
How great are you,
you little saver?!

300
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:15,021
I mean, the
amount you have is
exactly the budget

301
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:16,356
of my dream wedding.

302
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:19,359
Oh! You guys are so made
for each other.

303
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,362
Well, you're not suggesting
that we spend all of the money

304
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,530
on the wedding?

305
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:26,949
Uh, yeah!
Uh, yeah!

306
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:30,537
Look... Mon, I've been saving
this money for six years

307
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:34,040
and I kind of had some of it
earmarked for the future

308
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:35,458
not just for a party.

309
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:39,587
Wow! Hello, Mr. Chandler.

310
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:45,593
Sweetie, this is the most
special day of our lives.

311
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:47,136
No, I realize that, honey

312
00:14:47,178 --> 00:14:49,723
but I'm not going to spend
all the money on one party.

313
00:14:49,764 --> 00:14:51,057
Honey, um, I-I love you...

314
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:52,809
( giggles )

315
00:14:52,851 --> 00:14:55,895
...but, um, if you call our
wedding a "party" one more time

316
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,689
you may not get invited, okay?

317
00:14:57,731 --> 00:15:00,191
Listen...

318
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:02,068
we can always earn
more money, okay

319
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:04,404
but we're only going
to get married once.

320
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,613
Look, I understand

321
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:07,532
but I have to put
my foot down, okay?

322
00:15:07,574 --> 00:15:09,116
The answer is no.

323
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:12,537
You-you're going to have
to "put your foot down"?

324
00:15:12,579 --> 00:15:15,915
Yes, I am.

325
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:17,250
Wow.

326
00:15:17,291 --> 00:15:20,169
Money and a firm hand.

327
00:15:20,211 --> 00:15:22,963
Finally a Chandler
I can get on board with.

328
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:32,265
Hi, Rach.

329
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,641
Joey.

330
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,269
Hey, Rach.

331
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,479
Do you smell smoke?

332
00:15:38,521 --> 00:15:40,648
Uh-huh. I get it. Smoke, chimney

333
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:43,443
chimney sweep-- very funny.
Ha, ha.

334
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:45,027
No, no, no. I'm serious.

335
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,654
You don't smell it?

336
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:48,989
Something's on fire.

337
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,158
No, I don't smell anything.

338
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,077
Oh, you know what?

339
00:15:53,119 --> 00:15:55,121
It's probably
just your burnin' loins.

340
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,586
Hey, what are you guys
talking about?

341
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:02,796
Nothing.

342
00:16:04,798 --> 00:16:08,342
Hmm. Dang, this
coffee's cold.

343
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:10,804
Hey, Rach, do you mind
if I heat this up on your loins?

344
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:16,267
You know,
I cannot believe

345
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:17,351
you told him.

346
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:19,061
Joey...

347
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:22,148
So, I guess you bought that book
after we broke up, huh?

348
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,817
Uh-huh. Yeah, I did

349
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,984
because I wore out my first copy
when I was with you.

350
00:16:27,236 --> 00:16:28,529
Oh, yeah, yeah?

351
00:16:28,571 --> 00:16:30,573
Well, uh, when we were going out

352
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:33,075
I read tons of porno magazines!

353
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:36,120
Whassup?

354
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:40,374
Ross, how could you
do that to an old man?!

355
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:44,295
Excuse me, ladies.

356
00:16:44,337 --> 00:16:46,631
I'm sorry?

357
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:48,132
My massage client,
Arthur?

358
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:50,134
His daughter called

359
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:52,595
and said that some guy
that worked for me

360
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:55,431
gave him a really
weird massage
this afternoon.

361
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:58,476
I gave him an extremely
professional massage.

362
00:16:58,518 --> 00:17:02,104
He said you poked at him
with wooden spoons.

363
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:05,441
Well, okay, so it wasn't,
a-a traditional massage.

364
00:17:05,483 --> 00:17:09,320
But I did give him acupressure
with a pair of chopsticks.

365
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:12,866
And, and, I gently exfoliated
him with-with a mop.

366
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:16,661
Well, he's never
coming back.

367
00:17:16,703 --> 00:17:18,412
Okay, you just cost
me $80 a week!

368
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:20,498
Hey, you know what?
This is your fault.

369
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:22,458
You're the one who didn't move
his appointment.

370
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:23,793
Oh, it's my fault?

371
00:17:23,835 --> 00:17:25,336
You didn't have to massage him.

372
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:26,754
You could've sent him away.

373
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:28,589
You could've not rolled
Tonka trucks

374
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:29,966
up and down his back!

375
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:33,887
He said he liked that!

376
00:17:36,389 --> 00:17:38,349
Oh, you're right, you're right.

377
00:17:38,391 --> 00:17:39,809
I'm sorry.

378
00:17:39,851 --> 00:17:41,019
Dude...

379
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:44,022
What are you massaging
an old man for?

380
00:17:44,062 --> 00:17:46,566
His daughter was hot.

381
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:48,442
Gotcha.

382
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,114
( door opens )

383
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:56,075
Hey.

384
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:57,535
Hey.

385
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:59,370
Listen, um...

386
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:03,123
I've been thinking
and...

387
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,125
It's not fair for me to ask you

388
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:07,837
to spend all of your money
on our wedding.

389
00:18:07,879 --> 00:18:10,798
I mean, you work... you work
really hard for that.

390
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:11,758
Yeah.

391
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:13,259
Well, you worked for that.

392
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,889
Look, I've thought
about it, too

393
00:18:17,931 --> 00:18:19,599
and I'm sorry.

394
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,308
I think we should spend
all of the money

395
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,643
on the wedding.

396
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:24,854
You do?

397
00:18:24,896 --> 00:18:27,565
Yeah, I'm putting
my foot down.

398
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:29,108
( chuckling )

399
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:30,109
Yeah, look.

400
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,070
When I proposed,
I told you

401
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:35,239
that I would do anything
to make you happy...

402
00:18:35,281 --> 00:18:38,034
and if having the perfect
wedding makes you happy

403
00:18:38,076 --> 00:18:41,704
then... then that's
what we're going to do.

404
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:44,331
You are so sweet.

405
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,544
Oh, but wait.

406
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:51,505
What about, what about
the future and stuff?

407
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:53,883
Ahh, forget about
the future and stuff.

408
00:18:53,925 --> 00:18:55,426
So we only have two kids.

409
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,428
You know, we'll pick
our favorite

410
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,806
and that one will get
to go to college.

411
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,933
I mean, you've thought
about that?

412
00:19:01,975 --> 00:19:03,267
Yeah.

413
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:05,185
How many kids
were we gonna have?

414
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:09,148
Uh, four: a boy,
twin girls,
and another boy.

415
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:12,902
What else
did you think about?

416
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:15,989
Well, stuff like
where we'd live.

417
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:17,531
You know,
like a small place

418
00:19:17,573 --> 00:19:19,199
outside the city

419
00:19:19,241 --> 00:19:22,536
where our kids could learn
to ride their bikes and stuff.

420
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:24,288
You know, we could have a cat

421
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:25,999
that had a bell on its collar

422
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,834
and we could hear it every time

423
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:30,003
it ran through
the little kitty door.

424
00:19:30,044 --> 00:19:32,880
Of course, we'd have
an apartment over the garage

425
00:19:32,922 --> 00:19:34,507
where Joey could grow old.

426
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:41,848
You know what?

427
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:45,059
I-I don't want a big,
fancy wedding.

428
00:19:45,101 --> 00:19:46,435
Sure you do.

429
00:19:46,477 --> 00:19:47,728
No.

430
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:51,482
I want everything
that you've just said.

431
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:54,443
I want a marriage.

432
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:55,862
You sure?

433
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,947
Mm-hmm.

434
00:19:57,989 --> 00:20:00,574
I love you so much.

435
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:02,743
I love you.

436
00:20:07,498 --> 00:20:08,791
Hey, listen, um

437
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:10,710
when you were talking
about our future

438
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:14,296
when you said cat,
but you meant dog, right?

439
00:20:16,007 --> 00:20:17,508
Yeah, totally.

440
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:19,802
Oh, good.

441
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:32,523
Hello, Zelda.

442
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,860
Who are you supposed to be?

443
00:20:35,902 --> 00:20:37,695
The vicar!

444
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:40,865
Do you even know
what a vicar is?

445
00:20:40,907 --> 00:20:42,533
It's like a goalie, right?

446
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,035
Yeah.

447
00:20:44,077 --> 00:20:46,204
Look, Joey, it's
enough, all right?

448
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:49,040
You're making these stupid jokes
and these sleazy innuendoes

449
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:51,458
and it's, I'm not...
It's just not funny anymore!

450
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,877
All right, I'm sorry.

451
00:20:52,919 --> 00:20:53,920
Rach, I'm sorry.

452
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:55,129
Okay, I'm sorry.

453
00:20:55,171 --> 00:20:56,881
Maybe I can make it up
to you by...

454
00:20:56,923 --> 00:20:58,382
taking you roughly in the barn.

455
00:20:58,424 --> 00:20:59,466
Aah!

456
00:21:01,928 --> 00:21:03,804
All right, you know what?
That's it.

457
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:05,472
You want to do it?
Let's do it.

458
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:07,641
Huh?

459
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:08,768
That's right.

460
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:10,394
I want to do it with you.

461
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:13,397
Been trying to fight it

462
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:15,691
but you've just said
all the right things.

463
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,735
I-I-I did?

464
00:21:17,777 --> 00:21:19,195
Yeah.

465
00:21:19,237 --> 00:21:21,948
Oh, I've been waiting so long
to get on that body.

466
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,866
This body?

467
00:21:23,908 --> 00:21:25,576
Yeah, that's right.

468
00:21:25,618 --> 00:21:27,661
Come on, Joey.
Sex me up.

469
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:29,496
Hey, hey, you're
starting to sound like

470
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:31,540
the butcher's wife
there in chapter seven.

471
00:21:31,582 --> 00:21:34,418
Oh, come on, now.
Don't keep me waiting.

472
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,087
Get those clothes off.

473
00:21:36,129 --> 00:21:38,172
But I would keep
that helmet on

474
00:21:38,214 --> 00:21:40,507
'cause you're in
for a rough ride.

475
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:43,552
I don't want to.
I'm scared.

476
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:46,346
